BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:bad-ischl-2026-09-06@local-running-coach
DTSTAMP:20260905T131742Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260906
SUMMARY:Long Run — 20 km
DESCRIPTION:20 km fully easy on rolling terrain\; no fast finish after Friday’s 1 km repetitions.\nPace: Easy portions 4:25–5:10/km by feel. Uphill pace is irrelevant\; keep breathing controlled.\nHR: Use HR as a secondary check with pace\, terrain and feel. Ease off if response is unusually high or drift is excessive.\nRecovery: No structured recovery\; keep the full run aerobically easy.\nTerrain: Approximately 400–550 m ascent\, mostly comfortable Z2\; technical descending stays controlled.\nPurpose: Maintain long-run durability and trail-specific strength without creating a third hard session.\nIf fatigued: Reduce to 16–18 km and 250–350 m ascent if Friday was harder than prescribed.
CATEGORIES:RUNNING,LONG RUN
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:bad-ischl-2026-09-07@local-running-coach
DTSTAMP:20260905T131742Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260907
SUMMARY:Rest — 0 km
DESCRIPTION:Full non-running day. Optional easy walk and 10–15 min mobility.\nPace: None.\nHR: None.\nRecovery: Full recovery day.\nTerrain: Flat/none.\nPurpose: Absorb the previous week\, keep six run days sustainable\, and arrive fresh for Tuesday quality.\nIf fatigued: Keep the rest day\; do not replace missed mileage here.
CATEGORIES:RUNNING,REST
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:bad-ischl-2026-09-08@local-running-coach
DTSTAMP:20260905T131742Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260908
SUMMARY:Hm-Specific — 16 km
DESCRIPTION:3 km easy\; drills + strides\; 2 × 5 km @ HM effort\; 2:00 easy jog\; 3 km cool-down.\nPace: 3:31–3:34/km\; prioritize even effort and a relaxed first block.\nHR: Let HR rise naturally\; interpret it with pace\, duration\, drift\, and feel.\nRecovery: 2:00 easy jog between 5 km blocks.\nTerrain: Flat\, accurately measured route with minimal interruptions.\nPurpose: Build race-specific endurance through longer controlled blocks.\nIf fatigued: Run 2 × 4 km instead\; never compensate by running the shorter version faster.
CATEGORIES:RUNNING,HM-SPECIFIC
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:bad-ischl-2026-09-09@local-running-coach
DTSTAMP:20260905T131742Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260909
SUMMARY:Recovery — 10 km
DESCRIPTION:10 km relaxed recovery/easy running after Tuesday quality.\nPace: Usually 4:45–5:30/km or slower\; breathing and legs must remain easy.\nHR: Use HR as a cap/secondary check\, not a target. No threshold inference from HR alone.\nRecovery: 60–90 s walk/jog between optional strides.\nTerrain: Flat to gently rolling\, ideally under 120 m ascent.\nPurpose: Restore movement and circulation while absorbing the previous hard day.\nIf fatigued: Rest instead if soreness changes mechanics or pain is focal/worsening.
CATEGORIES:RUNNING,RECOVERY
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:bad-ischl-2026-09-10@local-running-coach
DTSTAMP:20260905T131742Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260910
SUMMARY:Easy — 13 km
DESCRIPTION:13 km easy Z2 on rolling terrain. Keep every climb controlled\; this is not a hill workout.\nPace: Conversational effort\; typically 4:25–5:05/km\, but slow further for heat\, hills\, or fatigue.\nHR: Use HR as a cap/secondary check\, not a target. No threshold inference from HR alone.\nRecovery: 60–90 s walk/jog between optional strides.\nTerrain: Approximately 250–400 m ascent on comfortable trails/roads\; descents smooth and restrained.\nPurpose: Maintain climbing strength and trail tissue tolerance without compromising HM-specific quality.\nIf fatigued: Reduce to 10 km or take rest if fatigue is abnormal.
CATEGORIES:RUNNING,EASY
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:bad-ischl-2026-09-11@local-running-coach
DTSTAMP:20260905T131742Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260911
SUMMARY:Easy + Strides — 10 km
DESCRIPTION:10 km easy\, then 6 × 15–20 s relaxed strides on flat ground with full recovery.\nPace: Easy running 4:30–5:10/km by feel\; strides fast but relaxed\, never sprinting.\nHR: Use HR as a cap/secondary check\, not a target. No threshold inference from HR alone.\nRecovery: 60–90 s walk/jog after each stride.\nTerrain: Flat to gently rolling\; save climbing and faster aerobic work for the planned weekend session.\nPurpose: Neuromuscular freshness without becoming a third metabolic workout.\nIf fatigued: Omit the strides and run 7–9 km easy\, or rest if recovery is poor.
CATEGORIES:RUNNING,EASY + STRIDES
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:bad-ischl-2026-09-12@local-running-coach
DTSTAMP:20260905T131742Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260912
SUMMARY:Long Run With Controlled Blocks — 21 km
DESCRIPTION:21 km total: 5 km easy\, 2 × 4 km @ controlled HM-support effort with 1 km easy jog\, then easy to 21 km.\nPace: Fast blocks 3:38–3:42/km—strong aerobic running\, not goal-HM pace.\nHR: Use HR as a secondary check with pace\, terrain and feel. Ease off if response is unusually high or drift is excessive.\nRecovery: 1 km easy jog between 4 km blocks.\nTerrain: Approximately 350–500 m ascent overall\; faster blocks on a smooth\, gently rolling segment.\nPurpose: Develop long-run durability and sub-race-pace economy while Friday remains only easy plus strides.\nIf fatigued: Move to Sunday if necessary\; otherwise shorten to 18 km all easy. Never force the faster blocks on tired legs.
CATEGORIES:RUNNING,LONG RUN WITH CONTROLLED BLOCKS
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
