DESCRIPTION:8 km very easy recovery after Saturday’s quality long run\; no strides.\nPace: Usually 4:45–5:30/km or slower\; breathing and legs must remain easy.\nHR: Use HR as a cap/secondary check\, not a target. No threshold inference from HR alone.\nRecovery: 60–90 s walk/jog between optional strides.\nTerrain: Flat to gently rolling\, ideally under 100 m ascent.\nPurpose: Absorb the controlled long-run work without extending the hard stimulus into a second day.\nIf fatigued: Take a full rest day if soreness or fatigue changes mechanics.
CATEGORIES:RUNNING,RECOVERY
STATUS:CONFIRMED
